	\
Noise Gate\

\b0 This brings up a panel which lets you perform a noise gate on the selected sound.  The noise gate works as follows:  \
\
	1.  First, you specify a 
\i threshold:
\i0  a minimum amplitude level which triggers the gate process.   The gate algorithm moves through the sound looking for a sample with this amplitude or below. \
	2. It then continues through the sound for a certain number of seconds (which you provide).  \
	3. If all the samples in this duration so far are below the threshold, the gate then continues through the sound, slowly reducing the amplitude size until it reaches zero (you provide the length of time needed to do reach zero).  If at any time it encounters a sample of amplitude greater than the threshold, the gating cutoff is halted and the gate continues through the sound, but at step #1.\
	\
